/-!
# The ATLAS permutation model of the third Janko group

`TauCeti.Sporadic.J3` is the subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 6156)` generated by the two permutations
`J3.a` and `J3.b` of the ATLAS representation `J3G1-p6156B0`, the images of the standard generators
of the third Janko group `J₃` in its permutation representation on `6156` points. That is the
index of the maximal subgroups of shape `L₂(16):2` of `J₃`, and the least degree in which `J₃`
acts faithfully.

The tables are the forward images of the files `J3G1-p6156B0.m1` and `J3G1-p6156B0.m2`: the file
point `i` is the point `i - 1` of `Fin 6156`, and entry `i` of a table is the image of the point
`i`. Products follow Mathlib's convention `(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`.

The presentation selected for `J₃` is the ATLAS presentation on the standard generators, of
orders `2` and `3` with product of order `19`, so its two generators are sent to `J3.a` and `J3.b`
themselves. All eight transcribed relators, the ninth power of the commutator in the convention
of the source included, evaluate to the identity there with Mathlib's product, although the source
reads its words from left to right for permutations acting on the right. Hence the presented
group maps onto the model (`exists_surjective_J3`), and both groups are nontrivial.

Neither the order of the model nor its transitivity, primitivity or simplicity is asserted here,
and the surjection is not shown to be injective.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3`: the permutation model of the third Janko group on `6156` points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.orderOf_a`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.orderOf_b`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.orderOf_a_mul_b`: the generators have orders `2` and `3`, and their product
  has order `19`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.presentationImage`: the images of the presentation generators.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: every transcribed relator of
  the presentation of `J₃` holds at those images.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.presentationHom`: the homomorphism from the presented group, whose range is
  the model (`TauCeti.Sporadic.J3.range_presentationHom`).
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_J3`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `J3G1-p6156B0`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/permrep/J3G1-p6156B0>. Forward image files:
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J3/mtx/J3G1-p6156B0.m1> and
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J3/mtx/J3G1-p6156B0.m2>.
* The same source, presentation `J3G1-P1`, for the relators transcribed in
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.j3Presentation`.
-/

